WEBVTT

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:40.090
This country was protected by the Touda army which belonged to the Grand Duke, who ruled the quarter beyond the mountains.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.160
Hurry and find it!

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.580
Search through that, too!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.780
All right, this is fine.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.970
Next!

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.620
Ani-ue.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.720
I was told you were looking for me.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:18.550
Ngan, take a look at this.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:26.300
It's some chichi mimic that was mixed in with the supplies headed to the Queen from here, the Grand Duke's quarter.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.260
"Chichi mimic?"

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.070
Why was a poisonous grass like that mixed in?

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:37.610
A threat letter saying that a poison was mixed into the supplies was delivered, and this was retrieved after a thorough search.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.920
"A threat letter?"

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.990
Who dares to send a threat letter to us, who possess the Touda army?

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.950
I don't know.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.910
Saigamuru...

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.330
Don't thoughtlessly mention that name!

00:02:55.330 --> 00:03:02.370
But some from Saigamuru have been known to rebel against the Queen as well as to revolt.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.340
Plus, there are rumors saying that they're after Touda eggs.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.810
Saigamuru...

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.870
Ngan, I will look into this using my own methods.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.470
Okay.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:32.530
Then I will work harder on training the men to better protect the Queen.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.700
The poison could already be spreading throughout this country.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:04:00.550
Behind the Door

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:10.020
Far away from the Grand Duke's quarter, at the base of the mountain to the east of the capital, lived Jone the honey man.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:16.500
Erin, who was now living with Jone, was preparing to move.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.800
There we go.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.090
You can stop there with the cleaning.  Help me out here.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.330
What?  But I still have the back room left.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.780
You don't have to clean that room.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.770
What?  Why?

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.020
You see, I've been hiding it this whole time,

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.040
but they come out from there.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:00.210
Scary ghosts come out from there.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.650
Ghosts?

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.770
Yeah.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.380
Really?

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.590
Yeah.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.750
I wanna see one!

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.860
I wanna see a ghost!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.100
Let me see!

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:22.090
Ah, no.  You can't, just can't!  I finally managed to trap them in there.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.300
You absolutely can't go in there, do you hear?

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.980
Now, come here and help me.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:30.490
Okay.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.990
Oji-san.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.590
Why are we moving?

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.460
Do you know what my job is?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.790
Keep the bees and sell the honey.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.960
How do the bees make their honey?

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:54.930
Um well, they collect nectar from the flowers and turn it into honey.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.890
When will those flowers bloom?

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.090
Spring!

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.430
That's right.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.710
But here in this area it will soon be summer.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:06.860
Look.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.070
Summer bells are starting to bloom.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.070
These?

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.400
Yeah.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.330
That flower blooms all around here once summer hits.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.670
It's my first time seeing these.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.320
Wait, but haven't I...

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:30.440
That flower is indigenous to this area.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:36.010
We honey men use that flower as a signal to move up into the mountains.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.020
That's the reason behind this move?

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.460
Yeah.  We chase after flowers.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.940
Is this flower's nectar sweet?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.550
You do the scariest things out of the blue.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.490
I shouldn't lick it?

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:09.500
No.  Lick that, and you'll suffer a stomachache for at least three days.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.990
It's horrible.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.370
Have you licked it before?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.480
Without licking it, nobody would know the result.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:30.470
The summer bells' pure nectar is poisonous, but tweak it a little and it becomes medicine.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.690
It can be poison or medicine.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.400
It's a neat flower like that.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.360
You know a lot of things!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:38.960
You could say that.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:45.830
All right, let's get ready to move Tocchi and Noro.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:46.980
Yes.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.670
I'm hungry.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:57.010
Let's eat a few, Ani.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.010
No!  Those snacks we received are thanks for doing something good.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.590
We promised to eat them with the little girl.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.440
Oh, that's right.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:37.800
The ghost room!

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.010
Oji-san!

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.930
Will Oji-san be all right?

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.290
I can only see his butt.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.250
Sorry to ask, but can you stay and watch the house?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:31.510
I need to go tell my nearby master that I'll be moving.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:32.760
Okay.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.440
Don't enter this room, you hear?

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.180
The scary ghosts are sleeping right now.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.470
Okay.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.230
I'm off then.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.030
All right.  It's sparkling clean.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.190
<i>The scary ghosts are sleeping right now.</i>

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.820
Do ghosts sleep?

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.610
I can't hear anything.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.900
Wow!

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.770
Why are there so many books here?

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:32.990
It's the same book Mom had.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.160
It has been a while, Master.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.170
You haven't changed all that much.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:53.150
Old guys don't change that much in just a year or two.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.070
Looks like you've gained some wrinkles.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.850
They're from laughing too much.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.550
This is good sake.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:10.520
It's sake made from honey, just like you taught me.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.720
I've got nothing more to teach you.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.300
You're already a full-fledged honey man.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:35.820
You must have something you want to talk about for you to have come here.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:41.780
I picked up a girl who was drifting down the river.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.110
What?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.110
Actually, I'm living with her now.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:51.530
She's a smart girl who replies with ten questions for every one new thing I teach her.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:53.760
Keep going.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:58.180
I'm hesitant.

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:08.740
Summer bells?

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.000
<i>What's this flower?</i>

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.490
<i>It's called a summer bell.</i>

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:27.000
<i>"...to  ...and  ...with  ...shine?"</i>

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.040
<i>"Indigenous to brae and mountainous areas with ample sunshine</i>."

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.000
<i>You can't read by skipping the words you don't know.</i>

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.100
<i>Okay.</i>

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.480
<i>"Indigenous to..."</i>

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.440
<i>"...and  ...with..."</i>

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.400
<i>I'll teach you.</i>

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:48.660
<i>Okay!</i>

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:53.230
<i>Every word per line holds a meaning.</i>

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.240
<i>This means "mountain." </i>

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.660
<i>Ah!  It</i> is <i>a mountain.</i>

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:01.960
<i>This means "flower."</i>

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.600
<i>This means-</i>

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.420
"Mountain...  Flower..."

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.210
"Capracide..."

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:14.380
Capracide!  I know this.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.110
Let's see...

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.170
"The grass..."

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:23.510
Hello!

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:25.060
'Ello!

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:27.270
Little girl!

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:32.260
Is she out?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.320
Old man!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.030
It's not safe to leave the door open.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:40.250
What are they going to do if someone decides to let themselves in?

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.230
Don't you agree?

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.350
Yeah.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.710
So the girl is a fast learner?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:55.350
Like raindrops soaking into moss, she absorbs everything I say.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.210
And how her eyes shine when she comes to an understanding...

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:37.680
Looks like your Tousana side is coming out.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:42.670
I've already rid myself of that title.

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.480
That's right.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:49.610
But, Jone.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:53.900
How long are you going to drag around your past like this?

00:15:54.990 --> 00:16:02.970
No matter how talented she is, she can't improve without a person to guide her.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:10.260
Like I taught you how to be a honey man, you should guide her.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.560
Ah, there you are.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.890
There she is.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:31.070
Little girl.  Let's eat these together.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.890
It's a snack we got for our work.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.610
We didn't steal it from others.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:42.070
Little girl?

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.130
You don't like snacks?

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:59.560
Looks like she's engrossed in the book.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.410
Let's wait there until she's done.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.830
Let's.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:11.310
Erin kept reading the book without even realizing that Nukku and Mokku were there.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:20.460
While remembering what her mother taught her, Erin continued to read the book on poisons.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.500
Ow!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.450
It hurts!
Ow!

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.120
It hurts!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.660
Ow...

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:32.490
What happened to you two?!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.210
Oww...

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:36.950
We ate those snacks, and our stomachs started to hurt...

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:40.550
Stomach hurts...

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.350
These are spoiled!

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.390
I didn't notice that.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:52.300
Me neither.  It hurts.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.200
What should I do?

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:05.650
The book!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.000
"Cure...  poison, poison..."

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.850
It hurts...

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:16.460
"Summer bells..."

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.380
Summer bells?

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:30.890
<i>The summer bells' pure nectar is poisonous, but tweak it a little and it becomes medicine.</i>

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:42.280
"Flower of summer bell..."

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.590
"The flower..."

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.620
I can't read it.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.700
How do I read this?

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:11.060
Hey, what's wrong?

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:15.340
Oji-san!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.160
Here, drink this.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:31.730
It's bitter!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.150
It tastes horrible!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:36.230
Drink it all, or you won't get better.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.180
Gross.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.590
So you've seen the room.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:55.030
Um, I'm sorry.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.050
You told me not to go in, too.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:02.520
How did you know that this book was about poisons?

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:06.650
Have you gone to school before?

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:11.000
No.  My mother taught me how to read.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:17.470
This is something kids in the higher level class learn when they're sixteen.

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:20.670
But I didn't fully understand it.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.340
I only read the parts I understood, a little at a time.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.460
Then...

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.880
I'm relieved to hear that.

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:38.850
If you understood everything written in here at your age, the reverends of the sect teaching at the school would all flip out.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:46.780
Um, how do you read the title of this book?

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.010
It says "Animal Index."

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.020
It's a book that documents a lot about animals.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.520
Really?

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:04.450
Do you want to become able to read these books here?

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:10.420
Yes.  I want to read all sorts of books.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:14.840
I want to learn many things, and I want to become like Mom...

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:33.980
All right.  Once we're done with the moving, I'll teach you between work.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:35.690
Really?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.280
Yeah.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.250
Thank you very much.

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:45.580
That's great.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:46.900
It is.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:51.970
I'll teach you guys to not eat spoiled food, too.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:55.150
At the summer mountain.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.000
"Summer mountain?"

00:21:57.510 --> 00:21:59.670
Follow us if you want to.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:01.760
I'll feed you guys at the very least.

00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:05.410
But I will have you guys work for it.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:06.720
Yay!

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.020
Yay!
Yay!

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:07.980
Yay!

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.150
We're lucky, Mokku!

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:10.700
We got work!
We're lucky, Mokku!

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.190
We got work!

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:18.730
Jone decided to teach Erin his knowledge.

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:26.960
And he was getting the feeling that life in the mountains that summer would be lively.

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:05.250
Erin!  We're finally moving to the summer house!

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.490
The food's good and the air's fresh.

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:14.410
It's my favorite place, located three-quarters of the way up the mountain, covered in fujaku and spring flowers.

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:19.160
You'll find lots of things you've never seen before.

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:21.500
So, what do you think?  Aren't you excited?

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:25.040
Kemono no Souja Erin.  The Platinum White Feather.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:30.030
The Platinum White Feather
